    "content" : "Last night I finally was able to program an ATtiny13A chip that I wasn&#39;t able to before. I previously tried using the AVR Studio software and a ZeptoProg II programmer but I wasn’t able to get it to cooperate. I found a great blog post on what to do and wrote a condensed version as a reference for the future. You can find that here: <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/dwaq/8239080\" class=\"ot-anchor\">https://gist.github.com/dwaq/8239080</a>. Also, this was my first time writing an actual document (and not a readme file) with Markdown and it’s amazing how easy it is to format documents. I would recommend it for any documents you may need to write that would have headings or included code.",
    "objectType" : "note",
    "originalContent" : "Last night I finally was able to program an ATtiny13A chip that I wasn't able to before. I previously tried using the AVR Studio software and a ZeptoProg II programmer but I wasn’t able to get it to cooperate. I found a great blog post on what to do and wrote a condensed version as a reference for the future. You can find that here: https://gist.github.com/dwaq/8239080. Also, this was my first time writing an actual document (and not a readme file) with Markdown and it’s amazing how easy it is to format documents. I would recommend it for any documents you may need to write that would have headings or included code.",
